  // ===========================================================================
  // COVERAGE ASSESSMENT & IDENTIFIED GAPS FOR PASS-2 RECONSTRUCTION
  // ===========================================================================
  gaps_and_pass2_notes: [
    "Pre-Columbian Mesoamerica, Maya, Lower Central America & Caribbean (Chapters 1-5, -10000 to 1519): OHM contains sparse pre-1500 boundary polygons; Pass-2 should rely on HydroBASINS Level 6 (759 JAGUAR basins across NA+SA), Natural Earth coastlines, Lago Texcoco (18th-c basin proxy), and published Mesoamerican/Caribbean archaeological site gazetteers rather than synthetic pre-Columbian borders.",
    "17th-century gap (1600-1700) in colonial sub-administration: DECM covers 1521-1600 (Relaciones Geográficas 1577-1585, Suma de Visitas 1548, Peter Gerhard New Spain) and HGIS de las Indias covers 1701-1808; OHM bridges 1524-1821 at Audiencia/Captaincy-General/Viceroyalty resolution (74 Nueva España + 8 Guatemala + 18 Cuba + 3 Puerto Rico + 7 Jamaica + 5 Bermuda slices).",
    "19th-century Mexico mid-century internal shifts (1836 Centralist Departments & 1857 Constitution states): 1824 (Bexar), 1836 Texas dispute (KCTCS), and 1900 (Lurtz 30 states + 328 districts) are downloaded as direct academic vectors, and OHM provides national borders + Quintana Roo/Baja California splits; intermediate 1849-1869 internal state creations (Guerrero 1849, Campeche 1858, Coahuila-Nuevo León union 1856-1864, Hidalgo/Morelos 1869) can be assembled deterministically in Pass-2 by dissolving geoBoundaries MEX_ADM1 / Lurtz 1900 districts.",
    "Non-Spanish colonial Caribbean internal parishes (1650-1898, e.g. French Saint-Domingue quartiers, British Jamaica/Barbados/Leeward parishes, Danish/Dutch Antilles): Island-level sovereignty timelines are well covered in OHM and CShapes 2.0, while parish/department geometry is well approximated by geoBoundaries ADM1/ADM2 (HTI, JAM, BRB, TTO, KNA, DMA, GRD, LCA, VCT, ATG, BHS).",
    "Minor geometry self-intersections exist in raw academic files (the_geom.gpkg: 34/1175; demografia_territorios.gpkg: 45/644; lurtz_mexico_1900_states: 2/30; lurtz_mexico_1900_districts: 5/328; bexar_mexico_1824_regions: 1/24; stri_panama_canal_subwatersheds: 5/54). Pass-2 scripts should apply shapely.make_valid() / .buffer(0) upon ingestion.",
  ],
